Tertius: keep an open compute encoder across a pipeline barrier to the compute stage.

MoltenVK 1.4.2 ends the open Metal encoder at every pipeline barrier outside a render pass, when Metal argument
buffers and residency sets are in use. Each compute dispatch behind a barrier is then a Metal encoder of its own,
and the GPU is idle for about 20 microseconds at each encoder boundary. On the station deck of Tertius that was
1.10 ms of a 24.0 ms frame (docs/research/frame-time-sweep-2026-11-11/addendum.md, sections A5 and A6).

With this patch, a barrier whose destination stages are the compute stage alone keeps the open encoder, when the
encoder holds only dispatches and no time stamp waits for its end. Metal fences keep the order that the barrier
asks for. The comment at MVKCommandEncoder::setBarrierInDispatchEncoder gives the three rules.

TERTIUS_MOLTENVK_STOCK_BARRIERS=1 in the environment gives the stock behavior, for comparisons.

The patch applies after moltenvk-execution-dependencies.patch, which adds _mtlComputeEncoderStages.
Upstream's issue 2893 proposes a similar change.

diff -ru a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCmdPipeline.mm b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCmdPipeline.mm
--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCmdPipeline.mm
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCmdPipeline.mm
@@ -161,11 +161,20 @@
 #endif
 
 	if (!cmdEncoder->_mtlRenderEncoder && cmdEncoder->isUsingMetalArgumentBuffers() && cmdEncoder->getDevice()->hasResidencySet()) {
-		cmdEncoder->endCurrentMetalEncoding();
+		// Tertius: a barrier whose destination is the compute stage alone keeps an open compute encoder of dispatches.
+		// Every other barrier ends the encoder, as stock MoltenVK does at every barrier.
+		uint64_t allDestStages = 0;
+		for (auto& b : _barriers) { allDestStages |= mvkBarrierStagesFromPipelineStageFlags(b.dstStageMask); }
+		bool keepsEncoder = allDestStages == (1ull << kMVKBarrierStageCompute) && cmdEncoder->canKeepDispatchEncoderAtBarrier();
+		if (!keepsEncoder) { cmdEncoder->endCurrentMetalEncoding(); }
 
 		for (auto& b : _barriers) {
 			uint64_t sourceStageMask = mvkBarrierStagesFromPipelineStageFlags(b.srcStageMask), destStageMask = mvkBarrierStagesFromPipelineStageFlags(b.dstStageMask);
-			cmdEncoder->setBarrier(sourceStageMask, destStageMask);
+			if (keepsEncoder) {
+				cmdEncoder->setBarrierInDispatchEncoder(sourceStageMask, destStageMask);
+			} else {
+				cmdEncoder->setBarrier(sourceStageMask, destStageMask);
+			}
 		}
 	}
 
diff -ru a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCommandBuffer.h b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCommandBuffer.h
--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCommandBuffer.h
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCommandBuffer.h
@@ -455,6 +455,17 @@
 	/** Insert a new execution barrier */
 	void setBarrier(uint64_t sourceStageMask, uint64_t destStageMask);
 
+	/**
+	 * Tertius: returns whether the open Metal encoder can stay open across a pipeline barrier. It can when it is a
+	 * compute encoder that holds only dispatches and no time stamp waits for its end. A time stamp reads the time at
+	 * the end of the encoder, so the encoder must end there to give the time of the work before the barrier.
+	 * TERTIUS_MOLTENVK_STOCK_BARRIERS=1 in the environment makes this false always, which is the stock behavior.
+	 */
+	bool canKeepDispatchEncoderAtBarrier();
+
+	/** Tertius: insert a new execution barrier into the open compute encoder of dispatches, which stays open. */
+	void setBarrierInDispatchEncoder(uint64_t sourceStageMask, uint64_t destStageMask);
+
 	/** Encode waits for a specific stage in given encoder. */
 	void barrierWait(MVKBarrierStage stage, id<MTLRenderCommandEncoder> mtlEncoder, MTLRenderStages beforeStages);
 	void barrierWait(MVKBarrierStage stage, id<MTLBlitCommandEncoder> mtlEncoder);
